Search is the fault origin: its calls to rate's GetRates path are held back about 2 s at the application layer, and the network counters show no change. The output is below.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "search",
      "fault_kind": "http_slow",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, count(*) n, approx_quantile(duration,0.5)/1e6 med_ms, approx_quantile(duration,0.95)/1e6 p95_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE (service_name='search' AND span_name='rate.Rate/GetRates' AND attr_span_kind='Client') OR (service_name='rate' AND span_name='rate.Rate/GetRates' AND attr_span_kind='Server') GROUP BY 1,2,3", "claim": "In abnormal period search's GetRates client spans take ~2.2s median (p95 ~4s), while rate's server spans stay ~1 ms."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT 'norm' p, service_name, span_name, count(*) n, approx_quantile(duration,0.5)/1e6 med_ms FROM normal_traces WHERE service_name='search' AND span_name='rate.Rate/GetRates' AND attr_span_kind='Client' GROUP BY 1,2,3", "claim": "In normal period the same search→rate client spans have a median of about 0.7 ms."},
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT 'abn' p, service_name, metric, round(avg(value),1) avg_v FROM abnormal_metrics_sum WHERE service_name IN ('search','rate') AND metric='k8s.pod.network.io' GROUP BY 1,2,3 UNION ALL SELECT 'norm', service_name, metric, round(avg(value),1) FROM normal_metrics_sum WHERE service_name IN ('search','rate') AND metric='k8s.pod.network.io' GROUP BY 1,2,3", "claim": "Network I/O and network errors on search and rate are unchanged from normal, so the delay is not a transport fault."}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {"from": "search", "to": "frontend", "evidence": [{"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, count(*) n, approx_quantile(duration,0.95)/1e6 p95_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE (service_name='frontend' AND span_name='HTTP /hotels' AND attr_span_kind='Server') OR (service_name='frontend' AND span_name='search.Search/Nearby' AND attr_span_kind='Client') GROUP BY 1,2,3", "claim": "Frontend /hotels server p95 is ~3.8s, matching its search.Nearby client p95 (~3.8s); normal /hotels p95 was ~13 ms."}]}
  ]
}
```

